debug('end add_signature: FA_SETUP12_BKCTRLPDCALSETUP');



debug('begin add_signature: FA_SETUP13_BKCTRLACCTGSETUP');
   l_info('##SHOW_SQL##'):= 'Y';
  add_signature(
      p_sig_repo_id            => '1431',
      p_sig_id                 => 'FA_SETUP13_BKCTRLACCTGSETUP',
      p_sig_sql                => 'SELECT   book_type_code              "Book Type Code"
,gl_posting_allowed_flag             "GL Posting Allowed"
,amortize_flag                       "Allow Amort Adjustments"
,allow_mass_changes                  "Allow Mass Changes"
,NVL(allow_purge_flag,''(null)'')      "Allow Purge Flag"
,allow_reval_flag                    "Allow Reval Flag"
,NVL(allow_cip_assets_flag,''(null)'') "Allow CIP Assets Flag"
,itc_allowed_flag                    "Investment Tax Credit Flag"
,capital_gain_threshold              "Capital Gain Threshold"
FROM     FA_BOOK_CONTROLS_SEC 
WHERE    date_ineffective IS NULL 
ORDER BY distribution_source_book, book_class, book_type_code',
      p_title                  => 'Book Controls Accounting Setup',
      p_fail_condition         => 'NRS',
      p_problem_descr          => 'No book controls accounting setup information found.',
      p_solution               => 'ACTION - Setup book controls accounting information.<br>
Navigation: Setup > Asset System > Book Controls<br>',
      p_success_msg            => 'Found book controls accounting setup information.<br><br>
Explanation of flag value shown in above table:<br>
1. Allow GL Posting Flag - allows you to create journal entries for your primary books. You cannot<br>
allow general ledger posting for your budget books.<br><br>
2. Allow Amortize Adjustments Flag - allows you to amortize adjustments over the remaining useful life<br>
of the assets. Otherwise, leave the checkbox blank to expense the adjustment.<br><br>
3. Allow Mass Changes - If you check the Inherit Depreciation Rules of New Category check box,<br>
you must also ensure you have checked the Allow Mass Changes check box in the Accounting Rules region<br>
of the Book Controls window, for any assets that you want to inherit depreciation rules.<br>
If the Allow Mass Changes check box is not checked, reclassified assets will not inherit depreciation rules,<br>
even though you checked the Inherit Depreciation Rules of New Category check box on the Mass Reclassifications window.<br><br>
Note: You cannot perform a mass change on the depreciation method on assets with unplanned depreciation.<br><br>
4. Allow Purge Flag - You must allow purge for the depreciation book you want to purge in the Book Controls window.<br>
To prevent accidental purge, leave Allow Purge unchecked for your books, and check it only just before you perform a purge.<br><br>
5. Allow Reval Flag - allows you to enter asset revaluation amounts. If you are adding an asset,<br>
enter the revaluation reserve, if any. You cannot update the revaluation reserve after the period<br>
you added the asset. After that, Oracle Assets updates the revaluation reserve when you perform revaluations.<br><br>
Revaluation Reserve = Existing Revaluation Reserve + Change in Net Book Value due to current revaluation.<br><br>
6. Allow CIP Assets Flag - If you have checked the Allow CIP Assets check box on the Book Controls window of a tax book,<br>
when you add CIP assets using the Additions API, the API automatically adds those CIP assets to that tax book at the<br>
same time that they are added to the corporate book.<br><br>
7. Investment Tax Credit Flag - The Investment Tax Credit (ITC) check box displays whether you claimed an ITC on an asset.<br>
You cannot claim an Investment Tax Credit on an asset unless it is using a life-based depreciation method.<br>
Allow ITC for a tax book in the Book Controls window and the category in the Asset Categories window. <br>
Assign ITC to an asset in a tax book in the Investment Tax Credits window.<br><br>
Note: This field appears only when you are setting up a tax book.<br><br>
8. Capital Gain Threshold - Number of months defined to calculate gain or loss amounts for sales of 1245 or 1250 property<br>
held longer than the capital gain threshold you entered for the book in the Book Controls form.<br>
Personal property is section 1245 or 1250 business property under United States tax law.',
      p_print_condition        => nvl('ALWAYS','ALWAYS'),
      p_fail_type              => nvl('I','W'),
      p_print_sql_output       => nvl('RS','RS'),
      p_limit_rows             => nvl('Y','Y'),
      p_extra_info             => l_info,
      p_child_sigs             => VARCHAR_TBL(),
      p_include_in_dx_summary  => nvl('P','N'),
      p_version                => '7'
      );
   l_info.delete;
debug('end add_signature: FA_SETUP13_BKCTRLACCTGSETUP');



